		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=5109&amp;p=37038#p37038"><![CDATA[
<blockquote class="uncited"><div><blockquote class="uncited"><div><blockquote class="uncited"><div>it have dual watch with the original firmware, but not dual reception.<br><br>OpenGD77 does not support dual watch for channels yet, only for VFO and temporarily: <a href="https://www.opengd77.com/viewtopic.php?t=1360" class="postlink">viewtopic.php?t=1360</a></div></blockquote>OK, thank you.</div></blockquote>FYI.<br><br>Each IF has its own analogue RSSI signal level output, which is read by an ADC in the CPU, hence in theory the hardware is capable of true 'dual watch' if one channel is VHF and the other channel is UHF, however I doubt the official firmware uses this advantage of the hardware and most likely the official firmware constantly changes frequency when in dual watch mode.<br><br>I think most users would be confused if the 'dual watch' functionality behaved slighly differently of the 2 frequenices were on different bands, compared when both frequencies were on the same band.</div></blockquote>Yes, I have this confusion too. I once asked the seller, and they said it can monitor both A and B channels simultaneously. I became interested in this machine, thank you for your suggestion.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=6826">BA7IQE</a> — Fri May 09, 2025 12:46 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
